<title>NEW ZEALAND: JF Asia Pacific details 10 pct buyback.</title>
<headline>JF Asia Pacific details 10 pct buyback.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jardine Fleming Asia Pacific said on Wednesday it had decided to implement an on-market buy back of up to 10 percent of its fully paid ordinary shares due to the substantial discount of the company's share price to its net asset backing.</p>
<p>The shares may be bought by the company through the Australian and New Zealand Stock Exchanges.</p>
<p>Up to 4.4 million of the company's 44.2 million shares may be bought back.  </p>
<p>The company said that the shares had been trading at a 9-31 percent discount to its net asset backing of $1.09 per share in the last year.</p>
<p>Jardine Fleming Asia Pacific shares closed on Tuesday at 97 cents.</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
</text>
